.TH "TEMPORAL.ZONEDDATETIME.ZONEDDATETIME" "3JS" "September 18, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Temporal.ZonedDateTime.ZonedDateTime \- Temporal.ZonedDateTime()
constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]Temporal.ZonedDateTime()\f[B]\f[R] constructor creates
\f[CR]Temporal.ZonedDateTime\f[R] objects.
.PP
This constructor allows you to create instances by directly supplying
the underlying data.
Like all other \f[CR]Temporal\f[R] classes, you should usually construct
\f[CR]Temporal.ZonedDateTime\f[R] objects using the
\f[CR]Temporal.ZonedDateTime.from()\f[R] static method, which can handle
a variety of input types.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new Temporal.ZonedDateTime(epochNanoseconds, timeZone)
new Temporal.ZonedDateTime(epochNanoseconds, timeZone, calendar)
.EE
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] \f[CR]Temporal.ZonedDateTime()\f[R] can only be
constructed with \f[CR]new\f[R].
Attempting to call it without \f[CR]new\f[R] throws a
\f[CR]TypeError\f[R].
.RE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]epochNanoseconds\f[R]
A BigInt that corresponds to the \f[CR]epochNanoseconds\f[R] property.
.TP
\f[B]timeZone\f[R]
A string that corresponds to the \f[CR]timeZoneId\f[R] property.
Unlike all other \f[CR]Temporal\f[R] APIs, it must be a valid time zone
identifier (either named or offset) as\-is, and cannot be a
\f[CR]Temporal.ZonedDateTime\f[R] instance or a date\-time string.
.TP
\f[B]calendar\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string that corresponds to the \f[CR]calendarId\f[R] property.
See \f[CR]Intl.supportedValuesOf()\f[R] for a list of commonly supported
calendar types.
Defaults to \f[CR]\(dqiso8601\(dq\f[R].
.SS Return value
A new \f[CR]Temporal.ZonedDateTime\f[R] object, representing the
specific instant specified by the parameters.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if \f[CR]timeZone\f[R] or \f[CR]calendar\f[R] is not a string.
.TP
\f[B]RangeError\f[R]
Thrown in one of the following cases:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]epochNanoseconds\f[R] is not in the representable range, which is
±10\(ha8 days, or about ±273,972.6 years, from the Unix epoch.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]timeZone\f[R] is not a valid time zone identifier.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]calendar\f[R] is not a valid calendar identifier.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Using Temporal.ZonedDateTime()
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] zdt = \f[B]new\f[R] Temporal.ZonedDateTime(0n, \(dqAmerica/New_York\(dq);
console.log(zdt.toString()); \f[I]// \(aq1969\-12\-31T19:00:00\-05:00[America/New_York]\(aq\f[R]
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Temporal.ZonedDateTime\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
